IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pca-types`
IMPORT `pca-evidence`

-- Tests for pca-evidence.l4 (Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 23, 24, 25, 36).
-- Expected values are read off the Act's text.  Generated by generators/pca_tests_2.py.

§ `23. evidence of custom is inadmissible`

`custom evidence in a proceeding under the Act` MEANS `Corruption Evidence Facts` WITH
    `the proceeding is a civil or criminal proceeding under this Act` IS TRUE
    `the evidence is offered to show that a gratification mentioned in the Act is customary in a profession, trade, vocation or calling` IS TRUE
    `the trial or inquiry is into an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or into a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS FALSE
    `the accused is in possession of pecuniary resources or property disproportionate to his or her known sources of income for which he or she cannot satisfactorily account` IS FALSE
    `the accused obtained at or about the time of the alleged offence an accretion to pecuniary resources or property for which he or she cannot satisfactorily account` IS FALSE
    `the resources, property or accretion are held or obtained by another person` IS FALSE
    `there is reason to believe, having regard to that person's relationship to the accused or to other circumstances, that the other person holds them in trust for or on behalf of the accused or as a gift from the accused` IS FALSE
    `the witness paid or delivered, or had paid or delivered on his or her behalf, a gratification to an agent or a member of a public body` IS FALSE
    `the proceeding is a trial for an offence under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the informer wilfully made in his or her complaint a material statement which he or she knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true, and the court, after full inquiry into the case, is of that opinion` IS FALSE
    `in a proceeding that is not a trial for an offence under this Act, the court is of the opinion that justice cannot be fully done between the parties without the discovery of the informer` IS FALSE

